l the prophet.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‹And afterward they desired a king: and God gave unto them Saul the son of Cis, a man of the tribe of Benjamin, by the space of forty years.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÖAnd when he had removed him, he raised up unto them David to be their king; to whom also he gave testimony, and said, I have found David the son of Jesse, a man after mine own heart, which shall fulfil all my will.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙYOf this man's seed hath God according to his promise raised unto Israel a Saviour, Jesus:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙewhen John had first preached before his coming the baptism of repentance to all the people of Israel.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙªAnd as John fulfilled his course, he said, Whom think ye that I am? I am not he. But, behold, there cometh one after me, whose shoes of his feet I am not worthy to loose.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book+§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙƒMen and brethren, children of the stock of Abraham, and whosoever among you feareth God, to you is the word of this salvation sent.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¿For they that dwell at Jerusalem, and their rulers, because they knew him not, nor yet the voices of the prophets which are read every sabbath day, they have fulfilled them in condemning him.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ`And though they found no cause of death in him, yet desired they Pilate that he should be slain.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙwAnd when they had fulfilled all that was written of him, they took him down from the tree, and laid him in a sepulchre.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ!But God raised him from the dead:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙzand he was seen many days of them which came up with him from Galilee to Jerusalem, who are his witnesses unto the people.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book+§chapter«first_verse ªlast_verse%¦verses–„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ[And we declare unto you glad tidings, how that the promise which was made unto the fathers,¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙµGod hath fulfilled the same unto us their children, in that he hath raised up Jesus again; as it is also written in the second psalm, Thou art my Son, this day have I begotten thee.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙœAnd as concerning that he raised him up from the dead, now no more to return to corruption, he said on this wise, I will give you the sure mercies of David.¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙaWherefore he saith also in another psalm, Thou shalt not suffer thine Holy One to see corruption.¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‡For David, after he had served his own generation by the will of God, fell on sleep, and was laid unto his fathers, and saw corruption:¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ1but he, whom God raised again, saw no corruption.¦layout ªlast_verse%…¤book+§chapter«first_verse&ªlast_verse)¦verses”„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙuBe it known unto you therefore, men and brethren, that through this man is preached unto you the forgiveness of sins:¦layout ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙtand by him all that believe are justified from all things, from which ye could not be justified by the law of Moses.¦layout ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙNBeware therefore, lest that come upon you, which is spoken of in the prophets;¦layout ªlast_verse(„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines“‚¤textÙ-Behold, ye despisers, and wonder, and perish:¦layout ‚¤text¿For I work a work in your days,¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙKA work which ye shall in no wise believe